{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nCites re-measured on origin/main 403719c01ce (base 083620b0 drifted).\n\n`src/rebar/_store/hlc.py:42` reads `REBAR_HLC_NOW` inside `physical_now()` (`def :38`; override block `:42-47`, fallback `return time.time_ns()` `:48`; file is 111 lines). Setters: `tests/unit/test_hlc.py:33,39,48,58,67,77`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py:74`, `tests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py:96` — all in-process; `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py:521` and `:1585,1588,1589,1590,1606,1622,1663,1679,1697` — subprocess (ten keys total). It feeds the physical component of the HLC tick (`hlc.py:106,111`) and compaction horizons (`compact.py:181`, `compact_trigger.py:88`, `compact_txn.py:446`, `leaf.py:172`).\n\n`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:187` reads `REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER` inside `_maybe_pause_at_rename_barrier()` (`def :178`; file is 533 lines). Setter: `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_compact_process_death.py:101` (subprocess + SIGKILL); it pauses after the first `*.retired` rename (`:265`, `RETIRED_SUFFIX`).\n\nBoth reads carry `# read-via:` comments (`test-only-clock-injection`, `test-failpoint`). **No gate counts them.** `make lint` runs `scripts/check_config_reads.py` and `check_config_ownership.py` (`Makefile:299-300`), but those police config-*schema dataclass fields*, not arbitrary `os.environ.get` calls; neither marker string appears anywhere in `scripts/` or `tests/`. Removing the comments with their reads is therefore free.\n\nThe two names appear in `docs/env-vars.md:59,144` and `.github/mechanism-baseline.json:495,579` (`env_var::REBAR_HLC_NOW`, `env_var::REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER`).\n\n**`tests/unit/test_hlc.py:91` guards the read this story deletes:** `assert re.search(r\"\\bREBAR_HLC_NOW\\b\", source), \"the injected test clock must remain\"`. It will fail unless inverted in the same change — see Approach.\n\n## Approach\nMirror the store's injectable-callable idiom: `src/rebar/_commands/completion_verifier_run.py:76` (`clock: Callable[[], int] = monotonic_ns`), `src/rebar/_store/push_classify.py:88,100` (`sleep_fn`), `src/rebar/_store/reclaim_eligibility.py:19,45,57` (`now=`).\n\n- `hlc.py`: add `_clock: Callable[[], int] = time.time_ns`; `physical_now()` becomes `return _clock()`; delete the override block `:42-47` and the docstring sentence naming the override (`:39-41`). `import os` goes if unused.\n- `compact_txn.py`: add `def _no_rename_barrier(n_renamed: int) -> None: return None` and `_rename_barrier: Callable[[int], None] = _no_rename_barrier`; the call site at `:265` becomes `_rename_barrier(len(renamed))`; delete `_maybe_pause_at_rename_barrier` (`:178-195`) and `import time` (`:12`) if it has no other user — check before deleting.\n- In-process tests monkeypatch `hlc._clock` (`test_hlc.py`, the two js_safe fixtures at `test_cli_js_safe_integers.py:74` and `test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py:96`).\n- **Invert `test_hlc.py:91`**: it currently asserts `REBAR_HLC_NOW` *must remain* in `physical_now`'s source. Replace it with the opposite — assert `re.search(r\"os\\.environ\", source) is None` and that `_clock` is the seam — so the test keeps guarding the property, in its new direction.\n- Subprocess tests: new `tests/_child_hooks.py::child_env(env, *, hlc_now=None, rename_barrier=None)` prepends `tests/_child_hooks_shim/` to `PYTHONPATH` and sets `REBAR_TEST_HLC_NOW` / `REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER`; new `tests/_child_hooks_shim/sitecustomize.py` (runs at child interpreter start; `python -m rebar.cli` and the `rebar` console script both process it) rebinds `rebar._store.hlc._clock` and `rebar._commands.compact_txn._rename_barrier` (the reached/release file protocol moves here verbatim). The env reads then live in test code only, and `gen_env_registry` scans `src/rebar` only (`scripts/gen_env_registry.py:423`), so both rows leave `docs/env-vars.md`. Rewire `test_concurrency_regression.py:521` and the nine `env_extra` sites (`:1585,1588,1589,1590,1606,1622,1663,1679,1697`) through `child_env`, renaming the key to `REBAR_TEST_HLC_NOW`; `test_compact_process_death.py:101` uses `child_env(subprocess_env(), rename_barrier=barrier)`.\n- `tests/_child_hooks.py` is a new `tests/_*.py` module, which `scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_ci.py::detect_test_helpers` censuses as `test_helper::tests/_child_hooks.py` (filename-glob shape: the marker lives in the file's first lines). Open the file with `# mechanism-ok: test_helper tests/_child_hooks.py — replaces the production env reads REBAR_HLC_NOW / REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER (this ticket)` so `check_mechanism_delta --check` reports `new=0`. `tests/_child_hooks_shim/sitecustomize.py` sits in a subdirectory and is not censused.\n- Regenerate `docs/env-vars.md`; run `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` (drops the two now-stale `env_var` rows at `.github/mechanism-baseline.json:495,579`; precedent commit `81da792`) and commit the shrunken baseline in the same change. This is the sanctioned drain path: removing a mechanism buckets as `stale` and always passes.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_store/hlc.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py`, new `tests/_child_hooks.py` and `tests/_child_hooks_shim/sitecustomize.py`, `tests/unit/test_hlc.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py`, `tests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py`, `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py`, `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_compact_process_death.py`, `docs/env-vars.md`, `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`. Out of scope: `REBAR_RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP` (reconciler epic), every other env read in `src/rebar`, and the HLC tick / compaction-horizon logic itself — `hlc.py:106,111`, `compact.py:181`, `compact_trigger.py:88`, `compact_txn.py:446`, `leaf.py:172` keep calling `physical_now()` unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_hlc.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py tests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py -q`.\n- `pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_compact_process_death.py -q` (child reaches the barrier via the shim; SIGKILL recovery unchanged).\n- `pytest tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py -k hlc -q`, `-k skew -q`, `-k scenario -q`.\n- Edge: `REBAR_HLC_NOW=1 rebar create task t` in a scratch repo → the ticket timestamp is wall-clock (the variable is ignored); `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check`; `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` reports `new=0`; `python scripts/check_orphaned_load.py` clean after the SIGKILL test.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AC1 `git grep -n 'REBAR_HLC_NOW\\|REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER' -- src` is **empty**, and `docs/env-vars.md` has neither row. Pre-state to confirm before implementing: the grep returns **5 hits** (`hlc.py:19,39,42`, `compact_txn.py:180,187`) and the doc rows sit at `:59` and `:144` — if either is already absent, stop and re-scope. (BRE alternation is deliberate: do not rewrite as `-E` with `\\b`, which `git grep` ignores, silently matching nothing and passing vacuously.)\n- [ ] AC2 `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` no longer contains `env_var::REBAR_HLC_NOW` or `env_var::REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER` (present today at `:495`, `:579`), `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` reports `new=0`, and `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py::test_the_committed_baseline_matches_the_live_tree` is green. The two-row deletion is the falsifiable part; `new=0` alone is the repo's default state and proves nothing on its own.\n- [ ] AC3 `tests/unit/test_hlc.py` still asserts the clock seam, in its inverted form: the source of `physical_now` contains no `os.environ` read and `_clock` is the injection point. (Today `:91` asserts the opposite.)\n- [ ] AC4 `make verify` green."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793424281949518138,"uuid":"fed43635-a964-4c0c-ab37-c592bbb2fcdf"}